usage: lavatune [-h] [--version] [--config CONFIG]
                [--theme {soft-afterglow,cool-dense,mono-blocks}]
                [--list-themes] [--list-backends] [--list-profiles]
                [--profile {power-save,atlas,responsive}]
                [--content-mode {auto,music,speech,book}]
                [--backend {auto,pipewire,pulse,ffmpeg,sox}]
                [--analysis {atlas,bands}] [--source SOURCE] [--show-stats]
                [--no-stats] [--compact-tile]
                [--max-visual-width MAX_VISUAL_WIDTH]
                [--max-visual-height MAX_VISUAL_HEIGHT] [--demo]
                [--renderer {tui,canvas,window,kitty}] [--canvas] [--window]
                [--doctor] [--no-audio-probe] [--trace-once SECONDS]
                [--trace-output TRACE_OUTPUT] [--motion-analysis SECONDS]
                [--motion-output MOTION_OUTPUT]

A local-first terminal and desktop acoustic organism for Linux and macOS.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --config CONFIG       Path to a TOML config override.
  --theme {soft-afterglow,cool-dense,mono-blocks}
                        Built-in theme to use without a config file.
  --list-themes         List built-in themes and exit.
  --list-backends       List supported audio backends and exit.
  --list-profiles       List runtime power profiles and exit.
  --profile {power-save,atlas,responsive}
                        Runtime profile for latency and CPU usage.
  --content-mode {auto,music,speech,book}
                        Force audio response tuning instead of auto-detecting
                        content.
  --backend {auto,pipewire,pulse,ffmpeg,sox}
                        Audio backend override.
  --analysis {atlas,bands}
                        Audio analysis model override.
  --source SOURCE       Explicit audio monitor/source name for your Linux
                        audio stack.
  --show-stats          Show backend/profile status in the terminal footer at
                        startup.
  --no-stats            Hide live analysis stats.
  --compact-tile        Keep the visual field small inside a larger terminal
                        tile.
  --max-visual-width MAX_VISUAL_WIDTH
                        Maximum visual field width in terminal columns.
  --max-visual-height MAX_VISUAL_HEIGHT
                        Maximum visual field height in terminal rows.
  --demo                Run without live audio using a synthetic signal.
  --renderer {tui,canvas,window,kitty}
                        Presentation renderer: terminal-native tui (default),
                        Kitty/Ghostty pixel wax, experimental canvas, or
                        standalone window.
  --canvas              Compatibility alias for --renderer canvas.
  --window              Open standalone floating window renderer.
  --doctor              Check the local environment and audio path, then exit.
  --no-audio-probe      With --doctor, skip the short live PCM probe.
  --trace-once SECONDS  Capture local feature values for one bounded pass,
                        then exit (5-600 seconds; no audio is recorded).
  --trace-output TRACE_OUTPUT
                        Feature-trace path (default: /tmp/lavatune-
                        trace.json).
  --motion-analysis SECONDS
                        Analyze live production motion for one bounded pass,
                        then exit (5-600 seconds; no PCM is stored).
  --motion-output MOTION_OUTPUT
                        Motion-analysis path (default: /tmp/lavatune-
                        motion.json).
